WEBVTT

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:14.240
The killer pandemic is rapidly
spreading throughout the world.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:20.160
Our government as well as other countries are collapsing
as they do not have any solutions to this outbreak.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.040
In this country alone, the pandemic has claimed

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.250
over two million lives.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:29.130
Due to the infectious nature of this disease and lack of help from the government,

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.340
{overlap}I'm all sweaty.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.500
{overlap}Yeah, me too.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.630
{overlap}A bath! A bath!

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.380
the number of victims is projected to double in the next one or two days.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.380
{overlap}I'm drenched too.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:37.760
{overlap}Don't look!

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.350
{overlap}You don't need to be so shy!

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.470
We've also taken heavy casualties while trying to keep this show on air.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.180
{overlap}This isn't about being shy!

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:44.230
Our team will be evacuating to an offshore facility

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:47.100
to prevent further casualties from this killer disease.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.860
This will be our final broadcast for now.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.070
{overlap}Hurry up and come in!

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:52.990
{overlap}Miyamoto!

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:57.200
Farewell, everyone. I wish you the best of luck.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:54.400
{overlap}Hurry, hurry!

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:33.320
Yureta Genjitsukan Nakushita Mama de

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:33.320
As I lose my already shaken touch with reality,

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:38.360
Gareki no Youni Tsumikasanaru

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:38.360
my emotions pile up like fallen debris

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:42.660
Kono Kanshou wa Doko e Yuku

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:42.660
Where do they think they're going?

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.910
Tsuieta Kibou Kakae

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.910
With my crushed hope in tow,

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:52.880
Akai Ame o Harai Hashitta Muchuu ni

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:52.880
I ran straight through the bloody rain

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:59.550
Kuzureta Kanjou no Hate ni

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:59.550
After my emotions come spilling out,

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:00.850
Nani o Miru

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:00.850
what will I see?

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:02.140
Nani ga Aru

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:02.140
What will I have?

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.810
Mada Shiranai

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.810
I still don't know

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:09.690
Hakanai Subete no Minori wa

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:09.690
But in this silence,

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.230
Tada Muon ni Me no Mae ni

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.230
all of the shallow things I could gain

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:19.280
Hirogari Tsudzuketa

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:19.280
lie endlessly before me

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.130
This feels great!

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:37.920
It's like I'm going to melt!

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.010
This is shampoo... right?

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:48.430
Woah, teach... yours are huge!

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.730
Yeah, I get that a lot.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:53.980
Dammit! She said that so confidently.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:01.110
D-Don't! Miyamoto!

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.410
It's not like we're in a steamy eroge...

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:09.000
Why are we taking a bath together?!

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:11.210
You know why, don't you, Takagi?

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.750
Yeah, I guess...

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.420
But considering our situation,

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.090
we shouldn't be letting our guard down like this.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.140
That sound was more pleasant than I had expected.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:30.680
With an attractive voice like that, any male would...

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.070
Argh, she still sounds mature...

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:45.490
Sounds like they're having fun.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.410
Wanna go peek on them like real men should?

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:50.500
I don't wanna die yet.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:54.460
We're kinda screwed if this turns out to be empty.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:55.880
There's something in there.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:58.800
We found the ammo, so there has to be.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:03:59.920
Well, either way...

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:01.260
Let's give it a go.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:04.680
One, two, and three!

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.520
That hurt...

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.600
Hey, Hirano!

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:20.320
I knew it!

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:24.070
Ms. Shizuka said her friend lives here, right?

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.570
What does her friend do with these?!

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.950
What's wrong?

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.250
Someone's probably talking behind my back.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:32.910
Who?

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.130
I don't have that many friends,

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.460
so it's probably...

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:44.550
Springfield M1A1 Super Match, eh?

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:50.470
It's semi-auto which is fine, because the M14 series' full-auto is just a waste of bullets anyway.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.470
Umm, Hirano?

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.980
The magazine holds twenty rounds.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.940
This is fucking illegal in Japan!

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.940
Hey... Hirano!

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:58.860
Knight's SR-25 Enhanced match rifle!

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.940
Wait, you can't get these in Japan,

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:04.240
so it must be a modified AR-10!

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.320
The other one in the locker is a crossbow!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.620
It's a descendant of one that Robin Hood used!

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.910
A Barnett Wildcat C5!

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:15.080
It's made in Britain! You can even kill a bear with this thing!

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.420
That's an Ithaca M-37 riot shotgun!

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.710
It's an awesome gun made by the Americans!

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:23.420
It played a huge role in the Vietnam war!

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.380
Cool...

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:32.060
Even if it's not loaded, don't point it at someone!

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.600
The only ones you should be pointing it at are...

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:36.140
Them, huh?

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:40.310
I hope that's all I'll have to point it at.

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:41.820
You know that's not possible.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.730
It's only gonna get worse.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:50.820
In a war like this, there's no surrendering or negotiations or shit like that.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:53.080
Yeah, you're right...

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:54.330
That's why...

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.210
Another set of big ones over here!

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:02.880
Komuro, give me a hand, will ya?

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.300
It's a pain in the ass to load the clips.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.090
Have you done this before with air guns?

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:10.430
Nah, with real guns.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:12.560
You've held a real one before?!

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:14.430
When I went to America...

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:21.310
I got trained for a whole month by a
professional instructor from Blackwater.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.730
He used to be a Delta Force captain!

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:29.950
You're only an expert when it comes to this kind of thing, eh?

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.910
I'm so glad that we're on the same side.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:38.000
By the way, who the hell is Ms. Shizuka's friend?

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.500
These guns are definitely illegal...

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:43.000
Technically speaking, it's not illegal if you buy the parts separately.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:48.760
But it's illegal when you assemble it.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:53.970
She mentioned something about her friend being in the special forces, SAT...

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.470
Everything's fine if you work for the police, huh?

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.560
Well, we know that this isn't just your average citizen.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:04.110
Police officers that aren't married
usually have to live in dormitories.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:06.360
But if she can afford to rent a place like this...

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.360
Either her parents are rich,

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.740
or the man she's dating is rich,

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.410
or maybe she's involved in some serious shit.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.660
They're being too noisy...

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:22.000
It's fine.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:27.000
They react to noise, but the noise is all coming from...

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.590
Get away from anyone dangerous,

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:34.180
even if they're your family members.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:37.600
I won't let anyone who's been attacked or is injured through here.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:42.310
A lockdown is in effect here at western Tokonou city.

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:46.440
However, as this pandemic spreads throughout the world,

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:51.570
one in ten people are doubting the effectiveness of these lockdowns.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:08:01.370
Those of us that were left behind due to lack of transportation to our offshore facility

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:04.500
will continue to report on the current situation in Tokonou city through satellite communications.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.000
What do you mean when you tell us to just do whatever?!

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:09.210
What about the backup from the prefectural headquarters?

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:12.760
Communications were cut off?!

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:13.880
Dammit!

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:17.890
Sir, at this rate, the barricade isn't going to hold.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:20.270
Well, that's a given.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:25.310
We don't have enough people and some of the men here are normally office workers.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.690
But!

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.940
We've received an order from above.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:34.280
We're permitted to do anything to maintain order.

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:36.700
It seems that they're not doing well over there either.

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:40.080
The last order they received from headquarters was

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:43.620
to do whatever they could.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.830
Then give us an order!

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:48.460
Even if there's unharmed citizens over there.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:51.760
We're going to have to sacrifice them for the greater good.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.720
Our job is supposed to be protecting the citizens.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.060
Dammit!

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:05.350
It hasn't even been two days since this all began!

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:24.460
What the hell is this?

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.210
It's like a horror movie.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:32.550
I remember a scene like this in Apocalypse Now.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:34.800
What's that?

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:37.130
What's up?

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.220
Turn on the TV.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.100
This abuse of power by the police is unforgivable!

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.020
Unforgivable!

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:53.780
We believe that this killer pandemic is caused by biological weapons

00:09:54.110 --> 00:10:02.080
Right now, we're live at the demonstrations of those that are against this lockdown.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:56.780
developed by our government and foreign nations!

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:02.080
We condemn those that caused this killer pandemic!

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:04.410
Killer pandemic...

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:05.450
The nature of this group is unknown.

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.870
I guess they're talking about the living dead.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:08.330
According to these handouts from the group,

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:12.880
they believe that this was caused by the leak of a biological weapon

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:18.800
developed by the Japanese and American governments.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.300
Are you serious?!

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:21.640
Biological weapon?! Seriously?!

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:27.140
There's no way science can explain how corpses are able to move and attack people.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:30.770
Well, that would be the usual back story if we were in a movie or a game.

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:31.520
Or maybe...

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:39.780
I didn't permit you to shoot!

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.790
Stop it!

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.290
Don't shoot!

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:56.130
This child and I are still alive!

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:57.630
We're still alive!

00:10:58.260 --> 00:10:59.630
I-I beg you...

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:05.220
Please... Please save my child!

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:53.310
The despicable police have finally resorted

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:58.190
to indiscriminately using violence against the citizens!

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:04.990
This abuse of power by the police is unforgivable!

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:05.780
Hey, get that person on film.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:08.830
Unforgivable!

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.080
Unforgivable!

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:14.500
Stand down immediately.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:17.460
It's dangerous for you guys to be here too.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:23.220
Screw you! You're just trying to cover up the conspiracy framed by our government.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.050
I'll repeat myself one last time.

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.300
Disband immediately.

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:29.350
I refuse. Go away!

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:33.690
Go away! Go away! Go away!

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:39.070
We've been ordered to take any measure necessary to maintain order.

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:42.190
It's not exactly legal, but...

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:44.950
The order is absolute.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:47.990
Huh?

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.710
This is insane...

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:00.840
This is bad.

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:07.510
I think we better get moving.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:11.770
That's a bad idea. We won't be able to see as well in the dark.

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.310
Komuro.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.120
Sorry!

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:31.410
And teach, are you...

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:34.450
It's fine, isn't it?

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:36.160
Just for a little bit.

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:43.210
Kohta cutie!

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:44.460
"Cutie"?

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:45.970
Umm, uhh...

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:51.970
You've been a good boy, so here's your reward.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.400
We shouldn't be loud.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.160
Please go back downstairs.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:13.410
No way, I'm scared when it's too quiet.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:16.460
I wanna stay here forever...

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:21.080
Ms. Shizuka?

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:26.090
I just wanna stay like this.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.050
What?

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.260
Hirano, be on the lookout.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.470
Huh... Oh.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.520
Hang on.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:42.560
You're touching my ass!

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:45.280
Komuro, you perv.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:47.360
That's naughty.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:54.830
I'd be really happy if I did that intentionally.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:59.290
You'd be happy about what?

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.830
Ah, I mean...

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:03.250
N-Nothing...

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:07.170
I was just, uhh...

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:11.720
Ah, there's three Takashi's!

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:12.970
Huh?

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:14.760
There's a lot of you!

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:20.480
Don't tell me you're...

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.810
I'm all worn out.

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:27.980
Everything went crazy in just a day.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:32.320
and I can't even contact my dad...

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:35.330
Hisashi died too...

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:07.940
Komuro?

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.150
Our late night snack will be ready soon.

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:13.160
It will be our lunch for tomorrow as well.

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:15.200
Thanks a bunch, <i>sempai.</i>

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:17.530
I'm sorry that I keep causing you trouble.

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:26.290
Eh?!

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:27.590
What's wrong?

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:30.300
What's wrong?!

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.510
Oh, you mean this?

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:34.970
I was unable to find any clothes that could fit me.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:38.390
I decided to wear this cloth until the laundry is finished.

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:40.640
I suppose it does reveal too much.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:41.600
Sorry.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:45.150
Ah, nah, it's okay.

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:47.690
But we don't know when they'll attack, so...

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:51.820
You and Hirano have your eyes open for us.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:57.990
I put my absolute trust in you two.

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:03.210
Hey, Takashi, listen to me!

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:05.080
Takashi!

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:07.330
I think you should see what she wants.

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:12.630
At times, girls enjoy acting helpless.

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:14.010
So that goes for you too, <i>sempai</i>?

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:18.510
I prefer my friends to call me Saeko.

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:21.930
Sa... Sa...

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:24.980
It seems you need a little practice.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:28.980
Takashi!

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:30.860
Hey, Takashi!

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:32.230
Takashi!

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:39.950
Pay attention!

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:47.330
Like I said, Hisashi was really sweet.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:53.000
That's why I really want to...

00:17:54.130 --> 00:18:00.680
Even when I felt lonely, he was always there to listen to me.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:03.310
Even when I had to repeat a grade.

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:06.730
But all you ever do is get upset about it.

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:10.690
Are you even listening?

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:13.150
This is really tiring.

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:14.730
Huh?

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:16.320
I'm tired.

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:19.660
What the hell is with that?

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:22.700
That's why you're so boring.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:26.200
I'd be an actor if I could look happy right now.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.420
You're always like this...

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:29.870
Do you expect me to listen to every little thing you say?

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:32.040
I've got my own problems as well.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:35.010
That's why me and Hisashi...

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:36.130
Shut up!

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:40.140
You bring up Hisashi every chance you get!

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:41.390
I'm not him!

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:43.180
And...

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:44.680
He already died!

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:47.480
After he changed,

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:48.850
I killed him!

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:52.480
Stop running away from reality!

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:55.480
We're still alive,

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:58.320
and we're gonna stay alive no matter what.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.070
No matter what!

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:03.370
So, stop talking about him...

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:46.910
Onaji Yume mi Kakaekonda

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:46.910
Sharing a dream, we curled up

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:56.000
Kayowai Bokura wo Tsukiakari Dake Miteita

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:56.000
with only the moon to watch over our fragile selves

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:07.100
Kokoro ni Nai Koto Bakari

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:07.100
I bore a feeling in my heart,

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:13.810
Kuchibashitte wa Koukai Shite

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:13.810
so I always regretted saying just the opposite

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:18.860
Bukiyou na Watashi wa

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:18.860
I can never express my feeling smoothly,

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:25.660
Itsumo Kimi wa Yurushite Kureru ne

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:25.660
but you never hold anything against me

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:32.210
Doushitara Doushitara Tsutawaru no?

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:32.210
How? How can I make my feelings reach you?

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:38.420
Todoketai Todoketai Kono Kimochi

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:38.420
I want to deliver my feelings to you, I do

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:41.800
Aishiteiru Aishiteiru

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:41.800
I love you, I really do

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:49.680
Kotoba Ja Mou Arawaserarenai Kara

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:49.680
Words alone can't express my love for you

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:57.520
Ima Dare mo Inai Heya no Katasumi de

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:57.520
So at the corner of a vacant room,

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:04.490
Otagai no Kizu Nameauyou ni Kisu Shita

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:04.490
we kissed each others' wounds, licking each other

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:10.120
Fureatta Ondo ga Tokete

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:10.120
If only our warmth could melt

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:19.460
Zutto Kono Mama Toki ga Tomareba Ii Noni

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:19.460
and stop the flow of time with our love at its peak

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:31.850
Are you sure about this?

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:34.890
We'll take responsibility for everything.

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:36.230
Please do it!

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:40.230
Are you serious?!

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:53.240
Screw you all!

00:21:56.370 --> 00:22:00.420
Dammit! The people on the other side have abandoned us!

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:03.960
Get away! You're going to get crushed if you come this way!

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:10.970
That's the way. Come back with the bulldozer once you reach the middle of the bridge.

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:13.930
You're permitted to shoot anyone that enters the area.

00:22:14.810 --> 00:22:17.310
This is an order from...

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:25.320
This is...

00:22:29.410 --> 00:22:31.070
If we keep going, I'm gonna...

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:33.910
Get a boner...

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:41.170
There's a dog barking...

00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:44.840
There's a dog out right now?

00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:47.260
But it's coming from somewhere close.

00:22:50.260 --> 00:22:51.180
Hira...

00:22:53.510 --> 00:22:54.600
This is bad...

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:08.990
<i>I thought that the world was already messed up,</i>

00:23:09.860 --> 00:23:11.820
<i>but I guess I underestimated it.</i>

00:23:15.200 --> 00:23:19.370
<i>This was just the beginning of the end.</i>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:26.880
This world is already...

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:29.420
Dude! She's a little girl!

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:33.430
No, <i>onii-chan</i>! I can't hold it in!

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:33.760
Damn, guess it won't work like it does in anime.
